Description: cast Linux audio or video to Google Cast devices
 Mkchromecast streams what the computer is playing, or a video file, to
 Google Cast devices on the local network. Audio is captured with parec and
 encoded as it goes; mp3, ogg, opus, flac and wav are supported, with ffmpeg
 available as an alternative encoder backend.
 .
 It can be driven from the command line or from a system tray menu, which
 finds the devices on the network, casts to the one chosen and offers volume
 and playback controls. YouTube and other sites supported by yt-dlp can be
 cast by URL, and video files can be cast with subtitles burned in.
 .
 This is the saulusprime fork, which carries fixes for running on current
 Linux systems: PipeWire, pychromecast 14 and Python 3.14. Sonos casting is
 not available; the code that drove those speakers is present but
 disconnected.
